{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And the name of the second was Tzelah.</b> Rashi explained that their practice was to marry two women, one for relations and one for procreation, and the one for relations he would give a cup of sterility. And he explained that Tzelah was the one for relations. And it is difficult for me, for afterwards it is written, ״וצלה גם היא ילדה״. And one may say that this is why גם is written — that is, even Tzelah, who was chosen for relations, bore a child, and the cup of sterility did not avail against her."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:52.592704089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}